Subject: Cantor Runtime, Process Procedure, and FPGA Specification Solution

Description: Durable solution record for the completed SJS campaign that followed WS-CTPR-010.

@ [solution_uuid] f2fa508d-d7db-454f-b2b0-1634654e59f0
@ [conversation_uuid] cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa
@ [baseline_commit] 272dfe7fffad0b048187bb6d082cca25ef3b1496

& [Problem] was insufficient authority and conflated candidate layers
  + pure CTPR forms existed but no deterministic runtime signature authorized behavior
  + Simula-inspired procedures, model-created stored procedures, shared inference, and FPGA execution were preserved ideas without canonical boundaries
  + treating all ideas as one runtime would have mixed semantic language, execution engine, model protocol, and hardware target authority

& [Solution] establishes three exact profiles
  + CDRA-SJS-01 defines an effectless in-memory reference runtime over existing CTPR forms
  + CPPE-SJS-01 defines an effectless Cantor Process Procedure machine-form, IR, lifecycle, interpreter, negotiation, replay, and fake tool-transcript experiment
  + CFLP-SJS-01 defines a non-executable FPGA eligibility and software-to-hardware correspondence contract
  + each profile has separate explosion, canonical identity, requirement set, registry, signature, phase lock, authority grant, and invalidation

& [SharedArchitecture] is intentionally narrow
  + immutable typed values, explicit identities and versions
  + logical time and deterministic transitions
  + canonical backend-independent semantic trace
  + separate proposal, validation, compilation, verification, admission, catalogue, invocation, revocation, and effect authority
  + model perspectives coordinate through named typed messages and versioned negotiated frames across multiple inference passes
  + FPGA is a future derived backend and not the SOP or process language

& [QuantitativeSurface] is inspectable
  + 40 CDRA requirements
  + 40 CPPE requirements
  + 24 CFLP requirements
  + 72 shared hard constraints
  + 20 pruning decisions
  + 7 opposite-edge explosion folds
  + 3 canonical specifications, registries, signatures, and phase locks

& [AuthorityOutcome] is bounded
  + future CDRA implementation may begin only with a separately claimed in-memory root and transition dispatcher
  + future CPPE implementation may begin only with separately claimed machine forms and normalized IR
  + FPGA implementation remains blocked until software proof, profiling, preserved target-specific source, new SJS authority, and a separate claim
  + this solution performs no runtime, parser, compiler, interpreter, model-provider, or hardware implementation

& [RejectedOutcome] remains preserved
  + no vintage Simula compatibility commitment
  + no direct Simula-to-FPGA compiler claim
  + no model self-admission or generated-bitstream loading
  + no literal shared hidden state or uninterrupted multi-model forward pass claim
  + no agreement, determinism, compilation, or acceleration represented as truth
